<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/pedantique" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3118444); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3118444&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1503051318" alt="Pedantique" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3118444)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/pedantique" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3118444); return false;">Pedantique</a></span></p>
<p>The reason behind this essay is in part so Forum Critique and general members will have something to link to when pointing out a lack of a narrative in modern drafts. Note that this is an essay, not a guide since a narrative isn't <em>required</em> to write a successful SCP. It can really, really help though.</p>
<p>Enjoy!</p>

