														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3573407">
									

<p>This is a great breakdown of narrative usage in writing SCPs. I can relate that when I first got into writing scips, I had a hard time differentiating &quot;narrative&quot; and things like origins and redundant interview logs.</p>
<p>But I think a bit more can be added to the beauty of 3008: It has great worldbuilding that really helps the reader visualizes the scenery (well this is not related to the main focus of the essay, but might as well add to the &quot;what makes it interesting&quot; part &gt;_&gt;), the odd behavior of the &quot;staff&quot; and it breaks the common trope of &quot;humans fight each other in a broken world&quot;.</p>
<p>Anyways, 9/10, definitely link in future crits.</p>
<p><span style="font-size:0.7em;">Edit: smol nitpick but you mentioned Zach's name twice</span></p>
<p><span style="font-size:0.7em;">Edit 2: yay feexed</span></p>

