			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3573962">
									

<p>Nthing this. We've talked about this in chat before, and I know there's a non-negligible number of authors who primarily start with the object and build a story around it. I personally have used this process for all but one of my SCPs so far.</p>
<p>It's definitely a valid method, though perhaps not as widely-used, and I'm sure there are people on each side that find it natural to do one and nigh-impossible to do the other.</p>
<p>A good narrative is almost essential for a success article nowadays, but I agree with Decibelles that this essay is too bare-bones; Lev seems to be saying that there's only one good road and doesn't really offer much help in the way of navigating said road.</p>

