			<div class="content" id="post-content-3576462">
									

<p>I guess part of what's throwing me off is that I <em>am</em> a new author, and this advice still doesn't work for me. Had this essay been posted 3 months ago, it probably would have been among the articles I read before posting anything.</p>
<p>I'm not saying 'narrative first' is <em>wrong</em>, just that it shouldn't be presented as something new authors need to embrace. I'm new, and if I embraced it, I would probably still be trying to write my first 'successful' article.</p>
<p><strong>ETA:</strong> Again, I don't think the article is <em>bad</em> (and I think it's cool that someone tried to write about this &#8212; as it's a super-difficult subject!) &#8212; I'm just concerned that someone's telling new authors (myself included) that the way I write (focus on the concept, then build a narrative from it) is a 'fallacy'.</p>

							</div>

								
