			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3576479">
									

<p>Hm &#8212; I don't want to pollute the discussion thread for this essay with my thoughts, but I'll just mention that while I think strong narrative can transform a 'meh' article into a <em>magnificent</em> one, I don't think it's <em>always</em> vital (some successful articles are almost purely just the exploration of a concept, with barely any story present at all &#8212; sometimes the story is just 'The Foundation found this thing, here's a description of it'). Also, I agree &quot;narrative first&quot; is a valid way, I'm just concerned when we tell people it's the <em>only</em> way.</p>

